Is used inside \fBApply()\fP to modify the result property\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::Interrelation\fP< dim >::ResultProperty (const char * var)\fR [protected]\fP"
Specifies which property will be written back to the \fBModel\fP once the calculation has been performed\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvar\fP the name of the physical variable which shall be modified by the calculation\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Method defines which \fBOperand\fP is associated with the result property of the calculation and sets the application level accordingly, ie\&. if the result property is an element variable the target level will be the element and so forth\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Call inside of the constructor of the \fBInterrelation\fP subclass to define which property shall be modified by the \fBInterrelation\fP\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
Errors will be reported if the target property is unknown to the \fBPropertyDatabase\fP or if the \fBOperand\fP already exists in the \fBOperand\fP map\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> bool \fBcsmp::Interrelation\fP< dim >::ResultWithinRange ()\fR [inline]\fP"
Uses the value range that Operands get for the associated variable from the \fBPropertyDatabase\fP to test whether the calculated result is within range\&. To modify the range inside the \fBOperand\fP, call on the public interface of the \fBOperand\fP class inside the \fBInterrelation\fP subclass constructor to avoid redefining the range during each call to \fBCalculate()\fP\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The method returns the boolean variable 'true' if the value ofthe tested physical variable is within the specified range\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Calls the \fBOperand\fP method IsWithinRange()\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Is called inside the \fBInterrelation\fP method \fBApply()\fP on each computed variable value\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
If the computed value is out of range, an error is reported\&. 

